# List of allowed SSH keygrips for gpg-agent (~/.gnupg/sshcontrol).
# Format: <40-hex-auth-keygrip> <ttl-seconds> <flags>
# Using 'confirm' forces an explicit pinentry confirmation prompt on every
# SSH/sudo authentication request, preventing silent privilege escalation while
# the JavaCard AUTH slot is unlocked.
#
# Obtain your AUTH keygrip with:
#   gpg --with-keygrip -K
#
# Example:
# 0123456789ABCDEF0123456789ABCDEF01234567 0 confirm
